# Build-time configuration for the packaged app. Vite reads this for `vite build`
# and bakes the values into the bundle.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notebook kernel runtimes: fetched from the web origin, not shipped in the app.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# AMS mirrors Pyodide and the clang toolchain into `public/` at build time
# (scripts/fetch-runtimes.mjs) so the web client serves them from its own origin
# instead of a CDN that Indian ISPs block. That is the right call for the web
# build and the wrong one here, for two independent reasons:
#
#   1. `public/` is copied verbatim into `dist/`, and `dist/` is the OTA bundle
#      in its entirety — scripts/deploy-ota.cjs zips it and manifests every file
#      in it. Mirroring locally would take a release from ~21.6 MB to well over
#      half a gigabyte, and every phone on the network would be told to download
#      it. The whole delta-OTA effort exists to move less than 21.6 MB, not more.
#
#   2. It would not even be a mirror of anything nearer. On a device Capacitor
#      serves the bundle from http://xceed.learning.app, its own local asset
#      server, so `${BASE_URL}pyodide/` resolves inside the shell — the bytes
#      would have to arrive through OTA first, which is point 1 again.
#
# So the app points at the same copy the web client already serves. These are
# the overrides AMS built for exactly this (see usePyodide.js / useCKernel.js);
# the trailing slash matters, because the worker concatenates directly onto it.
#
# Both paths were verified live before being set here. If a kernel ever reports
# that it cannot load, check these two respond before suspecting the app:
#   curl -I https://xceed.nitj.ac.in/pyodide/pyodide.js
#   curl -I https://xceed.nitj.ac.in/clang/clang.wasm
#
# This is the same reasoning as getenvironment.mobile.js, which resolves the API
# base to the live server for the same reason: inside the shell there is no
# local origin worth reaching.
#
# The host is hardcoded rather than derived, matching the OTA server's
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL. If it ever moves, it moves in both places.
VITE_PYODIDE_URL=https://xceed.nitj.ac.in/pyodide/
VITE_CLANG_URL=https://xceed.nitj.ac.in/clang/
